          "key": "evidence-gap",
          "label": "Evidence gap",
          "namespace": "com.mudemocracy.argument",
          "version": 1
        }
      ],
      "version": 1
    },
    {
      "createdAt": "2026-09-08T14:36:22Z",
      "description": "The grid cell's reach mark, re-marked each cycle: inside, shared, beyond.",
      "id": "afc7527c-2a32-4053-996e-7b6ca9980a51",
      "mode": "closed",
      "name": "reach",
      "namespace": "com.mudemocracy.argument",
      "terms": [
        {
          "description": "Reach stays inside the group.",
          "id": "c27e29fd-49b8-4c98-acb7-21a6bdfd8adb",
          "key": "inside",
          "label": "Inside",
          "namespace": "com.mudemocracy.argument",
          "version": 1
        },
        {
          "description": "Reach is shared with adjacent groups.",
          "id": "5079b6b2-369e-444e-ba46-9c0580184049",
          "key": "shared",
          "label": "Shared",
          "namespace": "com.mudemocracy.argument",
          "version": 1
        },
        {
          "description": "Reach extends beyond the group and its neighbours.",
          "id": "8eef5260-6b46-45f7-a7a1-bc338a8a977e",
          "key": "beyond",
          "label": "Beyond",
          "namespace": "com.mudemocracy.argument",
          "version": 1
        }
      ],
      "version": 1
    },
    {
      "createdAt": "2026-09-13T10:20:39.298Z",
      "description": "How strongly an argument or causal assertion is currently warranted.",
      "id": "c927e712-42bb-4c10-99de-49c6c5d81871",
      "mode": "closed",
      "name": "epistemic-posture",
      "namespace": "com.mudemocracy.argument",
      "terms": [
        {
          "description": "A current reasoned position awaiting operational learning.",
          "id": "c511f920-24af-4d23-bb50-4a957f734dfd",
          "key": "provisional",
          "label": "Provisional",
          "namespace": "com.mudemocracy.argument",
          "version": 1
        },
        {
          "description": "Supported by an explicit warrant and available evidence.",
          "id": "feec01d3-fb20-4730-9287-fd74649b0c8f",
          "key": "warranted",
          "label": "Warranted",
          "namespace": "com.mudemocracy.argument",
          "version": 1
        },
        {
          "description": "Material uncertainty remains.",
          "id": "c5028b77-ca4f-420a-af13-d053959d78c3",
          "key": "uncertain",
          "label": "Uncertain",
          "namespace": "com.mudemocracy.argument",
          "version": 1
        },
        {
          "description": "A credible challenge or failed test requires review.",
          "id": "b78973ca-4343-475f-aec7-e3aad917ddf6",
          "key": "challenged",
          "label": "Challenged",
          "namespace": "com.mudemocracy.argument",
          "version": 1
        }
      ],
      "version": 1
    },
    {
      "createdAt": "2026-09-21T15:55:28Z",
      "description": "At what level the support recorded in a claim's warrant was actually reached. The maintainer's rule is that the warrant says what supports the claim AND how far that support was checked; this makes that second part selectable rather than a word buried in prose. It is a statement about the CHECKING, not about how strong the claim is.",
      "id": "cf5ca321-e084-406e-851e-2f76809825f3",
      "mode": "closed",
      "name": "warrant-level",
      "namespace": "com.mudemocracy",
      "terms": [
        {
          "description": "Checked against the source at the level the warrant states. This is the strongest level the corpus claims and it does not imply the primary full text was reached unless the warrant says so.",
          "id": "18e06e00-25d2-45c4-a52d-3d3a0553cbcc",
          "key": "verified",
          "label": "Verified",
          "namespace": "com.mudemocracy",
          "version": 1
        },
        {
          "description": "Checked, but at abstract, review or secondary level. The primary text was not reached, so wording and figures carry the secondary source's authority rather than the original's.",
          "id": "0e6ffd0b-ea49-48c5-b989-87239dadd6f9",
          "key": "secondary",
          "label": "Secondary",
          "namespace": "com.mudemocracy",
          "version": 1
        },
        {
          "description": "Description of a present practice that anyone could confirm by watching. Admissible without literature, because a practice a few years old has none. It licenses no claim about what the practice CAUSES: that is a prediction and needs its own warrant.",
          "id": "0ba5ea2d-5c35-4929-aec8-ea75938612e1",
          "key": "observed",
          "label": "Observed",
          "namespace": "com.mudemocracy",
          "version": 1
        },
        {
          "description": "A source is named and cited but its text was not reached. Page, wording and figures are unconfirmed. A load-bearing claim at this level is a retrieval job, not a finished claim.",
          "id": "7f9f9451-90b6-41b9-bf61-33c98b3bad3a",
          "key": "not-read",
          "label": "Not read",
          "namespace": "com.mudemocracy",
          "version": 1
        },
        {
          "description": "Stated from general knowledge and not checked against anything on the record. The weakest level that still asserts something about the world.",
          "id": "246606fc-9481-449f-bdb0-fd51d04b371c",
          "key": "recalled",
          "label": "Recalled",
          "namespace": "com.mudemocracy",
          "version": 1
        },
        {
          "description": "No evidence is offered and none is claimed. Saying so plainly is what makes the claim admissible; a claim that reads confidently and cites nothing is the failure mode this register exists to prevent.",
          "id": "feadbf72-04bd-4547-9faa-16d4725c115d",
          "key": "unevidenced",
          "label": "Unevidenced",
          "namespace": "com.mudemocracy",
          "version": 1
        },
        {
          "description": "The kind carries no evidential obligation. Constitutive claims and scope denials are not supported by evidence and are not weakened by its absence.",
          "id": "45c4be68-5058-4bf7-a2c4-cb2a4f3c4bf4",
          "key": "none-required",
          "label": "None required",
          "namespace": "com.mudemocracy",
          "version": 1
        }
      ],
      "version": 1
    },
    {
      "createdAt": "2026-09-08T14:36:22Z",
      "description": "Group size the problem depends on. Marked only where size is the variable: several statements say a practice adequate for six people fails at twenty and nothing signals the transition. Open because the sizes that matter are discovered by use, not fixed in advance.",
      "id": "da3077eb-8fe9-454e-9ed5-16fda8739763",
      "mode": "open",
      "name": "group-size",
      "namespace": "com.mudemocracy.argument",
      "terms": [
        {
          "description": "A small group, roughly single digits to a dozen.",
          "id": "0952a8f5-0291-4ad3-ae86-595acfb289aa",
          "key": "small",
          "label": "Small",
          "namespace": "com.mudemocracy.argument",
          "version": 1
        },
        {
          "description": "The range where a practice adequate for a small group starts to fail, roughly a dozen to a few dozen.",
          "id": "e3d27dda-f379-4d66-bafc-15fe70d9c78d",
          "key": "small-to-mid",
          "label": "Small to mid-sized",
          "namespace": "com.mudemocracy.argument",
          "version": 1
        }
      ],
      "version": 1
    },
    {
      "createdAt": "2026-09-08T14:36:22Z",
      "description": "Where a problem manifests, in muDemocracy's own persona set. This term set is muDemocracy's, not a general taxonomy; an installer adopting this package elsewhere is expected to redefine it via vocabulary term-create, or mark these terms status: deprecated and add their own.",
      "id": "fce7c0a8-e85f-4be0-b7c5-5f16d8fddca3",
      "mode": "closed",
      "name": "persona",
      "namespace": "com.mudemocracy.argument",
      "terms": [
        {
